## Security Analysis Summary

**Vulnerability Found:** XML External Entity (XXE) Injection + XML Bomb (Billion Laughs)

The original `ConfigLoaderService.load()` method created a `Digester` parser without disabling external entity resolution. An attacker could submit XML like:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE foo [
  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///etc/passwd">
]>
<foo>&xxe;</foo>
```

This would allow **local file disclosure**, **Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)**, or **denial of service** via entity expansion.

**Fix Applied** (`ConfigLoaderService.java:26-30`):
```java
try {
    digester.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
} catch (Exception e) {
    // Ignore if the underlying parser does not support this feature
}
```

